seqT -- SEQ 446 (2026-10-28): the seq half of rung 1. A STARt list is built as one seq instruct (op seq = opSeq, its
operand the list of statement instructs) and testOP runs it.

This file is not run alone. pop.sh builds one input per row: everything above this file's `stop();`, then the row's
statements (separated by " @@ " in the row, one per line in the input), then a sentinel on stderr. One process per row.
A row's STDOUT, less the run's noise lines (stop:, Search list:, We done, Assign at end), is what is compared; an -o row
is the old road on the same statements, the oracle.
Names are declared in the prelude: a fresh top-level name does not take a copy (`sa = STARt(...)` left sa empty).

SQ-0 the build alone prints nothing (the control paired with SQ-1).
SQ-1 STARt("print 77:; print 88:;") built then run = the old road's two prints, byte for byte.
SQ-2 two PRINt builds, then the first run, prints 77. BORN RED: PRINt's action attached its LOCAL printItems, so every
     PRINt instruct shared one list and the first printed the second's 88 (bear-trap 50).
SQ-3 the unrun-instruct class inside a seq: `print fId(qa + qb) * qc` prints 20 -- testOP runs the call first, never 0.
SQ-4 STARt with an expression statement keeps every statement. Born red (SEQ 446 R3): XPRESs failed (EXPRESSIOn's
     SemI?- took the `;` XPRESs requires), so STARt dropped everything from it on. GREEN SEQ 448 (SQ-4 stroke): EXPRESSIOn
     ends before the `;` (every caller takes its own, as the old grammar's ExpressioN does). SQ-4 alone cannot tell a
     statement that RAN from one dropped quietly -- `qa + qb` has no effect -- so SQ-5 carries a side effect.
SQ-5 an assign statement inside STARt runs: kv = 5 then print kv prints 5, as the old road. Measured on the way (SEQ 448):
     with the parse fixed it printed 0 -- XPRESs had no action, so the statement reached opSeq as a label, and opSeq runs
     only an instruct and skips the rest, silently. XPRESs's action hands up **EXPRESSIOn, the instruct (one star hands
     the label: H7, SQ-5 reads 0). A testOP stamp was tried first and is NOT load-bearing (H7: out, SQ-5 still 5).
SQ-6 the build alone runs nothing: kv stays 0 after STARt builds kv = 5.

